From: meanaverage <18336095+meanaverage@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): configure decoder cap and wait for a key frame
 before opening

Let the host impose a stricter decoder cap through a validated public option,
counting active and retiring streams together. Keep retirement, byte accounting,
rate limits and frame completion inside the decoder rather than an external
wrapper which edits private state. Tabby configures a cap of 16.

Do not construct a browser codec for a delta frame that cannot start a stream.
A bounded map preserves first-key-frame watchdog behavior without retaining
access units; key frames, stream endings, failure and close clear its entries.
An exhausted decoder cap follows the existing failure path, without evicting
an active or retiring stream to admit another one.

Tests cover public option validation, admission boundaries including retirement,
bounded key-frame waiting and cleanup. Creation-rate tests now begin real streams
with key frames and drain tiny auxiliary pictures between openings.
